  "id": "COMPOUND:23337 - PROTEIN:1107",
  "verbalization": "Nanolobatin B is shown to have a target relationship with Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf through three distinct pathways, all of which involve the enzyme B-raf. The first pathway links Nanolobatin B to Arginine deiminase, which in turn targets B-raf. The second pathway connects Nanolobatin B to Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which is also targeted by a compound that affects B-raf. The third pathway links Nanolobatin B to Sodium-dependent proline transporter, which is targeted by a compound that also affects B-raf. These pathways suggest that Nanolobatin B may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of enzymes involved in protein kinase signaling. The evidence is supported by high scores (0.644–0.6467), indicating a strong and consistent relationship across different targets. The mechanism appears to involve the regulation of protein kinase B-raf, which is a key player in cell signaling and proliferation. The integration of these pathways suggests that Nanolobatin B may exert its effects by influencing the activity of enzymes that ultimately modulate B-raf, potentially through a complex network of downstream targets. The evidence is robust and consistent, but further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
